# The body of a file that has a start is entered by the run time alone, by the number of its closure. Its entry by value is no unit and has no bytes: the word of the closure leads to one stub for all such files,
# which takes the number of the start out of a word of the instance that the run time has written, and stops where nobody has.
# RUN: units-with-code f4:GenericCallEntry mechanisms=all
# CHECK: unit f4:GenericCallEntry fused into f4:ModuleStart, 0 bytes
# RUN(NONE): units-with-code f4:GenericCallEntry mechanisms=none
# NONE: unit f4:GenericCallEntry fused into f4:ModuleStart, 0 bytes
# PROGRAM-OF: ../plan/commonjs-file-has-a-start.ir
